# Frontier Atlas — monorepo .gitignore
# Ignores OS junk, editor state, and language build artifacts.
# NOTE: research deliverables — certificates, proof traces, verifier outputs,
# exact data, SHA-256 manifests — are intentionally NOT ignored; they are the
# auditable record. See the "Large artifacts" section at the bottom if the repo
# needs slimming.

# ---- OS ----
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ---- Editors / IDEs ----
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
.\#*
\#*\#

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---- C / C++ / native build ----
*.o
*.obj
*.lo
*.slo
*.a
*.lib
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe
a.out
*.app
cmake-build-*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/

# ---- Rust / Julia / Go (in case any solver harness uses them) ----
target/
Cargo.lock
Manifest.toml
*.jl.cov

# ---- LaTeX build artifacts (keep the .pdf and .tex; drop the intermediates) ----
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot
*.nav
*.snm
*.vrb
# (LaTeX also emits *.log and *.out — intentionally not globally ignored to
#  avoid swallowing solver logs / verifier outputs; clean LaTeX temp dirs instead.)

# ---- Secrets / local config ----
*.local
.envrc
secrets.*
credentials.*

# ---- Heavy regenerable research artifacts (REGENERATE-ONLY policy) ----
# See ARTIFACTS.md. Git versions the reproducible CORE — prompt, source, verifiers,
# reports, and the SHA-256 manifests. Bulky DERIVED output (proof traces, big
# instance/data dumps) is NOT tracked: it is regenerable from the committed source
# and its integrity is pinned by the tracked manifests. This keeps the repo in the
# tens-of-MB range regardless of how many tasks are worked. Keep the manifests.
#
# SAT / proof traces (e.g. Ramsey R(5,5): ~135 MB of these)
*.drup
*.drat
*.lrat
*.dratx
# Binary numeric dumps (e.g. Hadwiger–Nelson Kempe samples)
*.npy
*.u8
*.npz
# Large generated exact-cover / SAT instance dumps (e.g. Moore-57 extension_instances)
**/extension_instances/*.txt
# Convention for future work: put any bulky (>~1 MB) regenerable output under one
# of these directory names and it is ignored automatically.
**/generated/
**/_artifacts/
**/_large/
